The deaths command shows locally tracked NPC-caused player death statistics.

Syntax:

  deaths
  deaths here

The global view shows the top 10 entries in each of these groups:

  Players Who Have Fallen Most
  Deadliest NPCs
  Most Fatal Rivalries

The first group also names each player's most common NPC killer. The
second includes the number of unique players killed by each NPC.

Use "deaths here" to restrict all three groups to the cataloged area
where you are standing. Player kills, player-controlled creatures, and
environmental deaths are not included in these rankings.

The tracker records deaths immediately when they happen and preserves its
summaries across reboots. Its tracking date is shown in the command output.

See also: help combatbrief, help score
